  {
   "k": "10uo3fu",
   "en": "Australia was among the first countries to announce it was at war with Germany, on 3 September 1939. However, Australia did not make a separate declaration of war. Prime Minister Robert Menzies considered that the British declaration legally bound Australia, and he announced that a state of war now existed between Australia and ⟦0⟧ as a direct consequence of the British declaration.",
   "frags": 1
